https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/assets/html/plot2.html" width="100%" height="600" frameborder="0"></iframe>]]></content><author><name></name></author><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Plotly]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">The Anwar-Thaksin Deal: A Masterstroke or Miscalculation? | FULCRUM</title><link href="https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2025/the-anwar-thaksin-deal-a-masterstroke-or-miscalculation-fulcrum/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="The Anwar-Thaksin Deal: A Masterstroke or Miscalculation? | FULCRUM"/><published>2025-03-05T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-03-05T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2025/the-anwar-thaksin-deal-a-masterstroke-or-miscalculation--fulcrum</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2025/the-anwar-thaksin-deal-a-masterstroke-or-miscalculation-fulcrum/"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name></name></author><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Anwar Ibrahim, the prime minister of Malaysia, has roped in former Thai premier Thaksin Shinawatra as his informal advisor ahead of Kuala Lumpur assuming the ASEAN chairmanship. This might be ill-advised.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Fanning the Yellow Flames of Thai Politics: Not So Fast | FULCRUM</title><link href="https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2025/fanning-the-yellow-flames-of-thai-politics-not-so-fast-fulcrum/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Fanning the Yellow Flames of Thai Politics: Not So Fast | FULCRUM"/><published>2025-01-02T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-01-02T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2025/fanning-the-yellow-flames-of-thai-politics-not-so-fast--fulcrum</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2025/fanning-the-yellow-flames-of-thai-politics-not-so-fast-fulcrum/"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name></name></author><summary type="html"><![CDATA[A media mogul is attempting to rally protestors against the Pheu Thai-led government. The call to action, however, might not resonate beyond a small core of anti-Thaksin hardliners.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">How a Provincial Election in Udon Thani Became a National Battleground | FULCRUM</title><link href="https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2024/how-a-provincial-election-in-udon-thani-became-a-national-battleground-fulcrum/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="How a Provincial Election in Udon Thani Became a National Battleground | FULCRUM"/><published>2024-12-03T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2024-12-03T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2024/how-a-provincial-election-in-udon-thani-became-a-national-battleground--fulcrum</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2024/how-a-provincial-election-in-udon-thani-became-a-national-battleground-fulcrum/"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name></name></author><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Thaksin used a local election to stage a political comeback. While this reaped dividends, the key is to ensure that the needs of voters are addressed in the long term.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Rule by ‘Good People’ or Rule by Political Dynasties? Ethics and Moral Politics in Thailand | FULCRUM</title><link href="https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2024/rule-by-good-people-or-rule-by-political-dynastiesethics-and-moral-politics-in-thailand-fulcrum/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Rule by ‘Good People’ or Rule by Political Dynasties? Ethics and Moral Politics in Thailand | FULCRUM"/><published>2024-09-12T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2024-09-12T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2024/rule-by-good-people-or-rule-by-political-dynastiesethics-and-moral-politics-in-thailand--fulcrum</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2024/rule-by-good-people-or-rule-by-political-dynastiesethics-and-moral-politics-in-thailand-fulcrum/"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name></name></author><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Constitutional mechanisms originally designed to prevent power from slipping into the wrong hands have ironically fuelled the growth of Thailand’s political dynasties.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Visualizing Ballot Splitting in Thailand’s 2023 General Election</title><link href="https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2024/thai-parties/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Visualizing Ballot Splitting in Thailand’s 2023 General Election"/><published>2024-08-14T17:39:00+00:00</published><updated>2024-08-14T17:39:00+00:00</updated><id>https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2024/thai-parties</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2024/thai-parties/"><![CDATA[<iframe src="https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/assets/html/thai_party_all_candidates_vote_share_dropdown.html" width="100%" height="600" frameborder="0"></iframe>]]></content><author><name></name></author><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Plotly]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">MFP Dissolution: Inevitable But Not Inconsequential | FULCRUM</title><link href="https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2024/mfp-dissolution-inevitable-but-not-inconsequential-fulcrum/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="MFP Dissolution: Inevitable But Not Inconsequential | FULCRUM"/><published>2024-08-12T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2024-08-12T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2024/mfp-dissolution-inevitable-but-not-inconsequential--fulcrum</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2024/mfp-dissolution-inevitable-but-not-inconsequential-fulcrum/"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name></name></author><summary type="html"><![CDATA[The dissolution of the Move Forward Party conforms to a pattern of judicial bodies intervening to manage political outcomes.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">All Roads Lead to Bhumjaithai? | FULCRUM</title><link href="https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2024/all-roads-lead-to-bhumjaithai-fulcrum/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="All Roads Lead to Bhumjaithai? | FULCRUM"/><published>2024-07-22T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2024-07-22T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2024/all-roads-lead-to-bhumjaithai--fulcrum</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2024/all-roads-lead-to-bhumjaithai-fulcrum/"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name></name></author><summary type="html"><![CDATA[The Bhumjaithai Party is cementing its status as the quintessential power broker in Thai politics.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Thailand’s Grand Compromise Tested, or Back to Square One? | FULCRUM</title><link href="https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2024/thailands-grand-compromise-tested-or-back-to-square-one-fulcrum/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Thailand’s Grand Compromise Tested, or Back to Square One? | FULCRUM"/><published>2024-07-10T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2024-07-10T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2024/thailands-grand-compromise-tested-or-back-to-square-one--fulcrum</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://naponjatusripitak.github.io/blog/2024/thailands-grand-compromise-tested-or-back-to-square-one-fulcrum/"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name></name></author><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Depending on one’s perspective, the grand political compromise in Thailand is either collapsing or still remains intact.]]></summary></entry></feed>